ously ran conventions spotlessCheck but not test. Added an unconditional ./gradlew -p conventions test step to the existing gradle-plugins job, preserving inputs.no-build-cache behavior. A real standalone compilation failed with GC overhead limit exceeded at the default Kotlin compiler heap, so the command now sets -Pkotlin.daemon.jvmargs=-Xmx2g. The documented local command matches CI. Clean no-build-cache validation executed all seven regression tests with zero failures, errors, or skips.","commit":1,"disposition":"fixed","key":"inline:4287068923"}],"input_identity":{},"outcome":"fixes","request_digest":"cd7b21f5e27b22caafb181c75f985082307604d7a814249b9213da4c5fa82079","schema":2},"download_sha256":"0b6f191276d42a6db98a5f72efbaf477f793c1edc6e10dfd5e31b5e9c9c5b384","frozen_sha":"16bd05cc5f11283e60da5870b883b5a69741fc70","pr":20625,"publication_eligible":false,"repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","request_digest":"cd7b21f5e27b22caafb181c75f985082307604d7a814249b9213da4c5fa82079","request_id":"86630fd0785548288e4edd91cfb7b0e8","run_attempt":1,"run_id":38790690799,"schema":2,"scope":"Structural/Git verification only. No target code or tests are executed.","server_artifact_digest":"sha256:0b6f191276d42a6db98a5f72efbaf477f793c1edc6e10dfd5e31b5e9c9c5b384","verification":"verified","verification_run":{"attempt":1,"id":38793212771},"workflow_revision":"1a211828aa1a2b731f5e9140623b5945a0dbdb6d"},"request":{"authorized_actor_id":218610,"baseline_review_ids":[5538375750],"budgets":{"max_iterations":5,"propagation_seconds":120,"retention_days":14,"worker_timeout_minutes":30},"commit_author":{"id":218610,"login":"trask"},"findings":[{"body":"<!-- ccr-overview-v2 -->\n\n### \ud83d\udd35 Needs a closer look\n\nShared Gradle lifecycle wiring needs human validation, and the new regression tests are not run by PR CI.\n\n<details open>\n<summary><strong>1 open finding</strong></summary>\n\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Conventions regression tests are not run in PR CI](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation/pull/20625#discussion_r4287068923) \u00b7 New\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>What changed in this PR</strong></summary>\n\nIntroduces reusable suite-owned Gradle test executions, with gRPC javaagent as the initial migration.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Adds shared execution configuration and telemetry metadata composition.\n- Migrates gRPC\u2019s four variants while retaining existing task names.\n- Adds infrastructure tests and contributor documentation.\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| instrumentation/\u200bgrpc-1.6/\u200bjavaagent/\u200bbuild.gradle.kts | Migrates variants to suite-owned executions. |\r\n| docs/\u200bcontributing/\u200brunning-tests.md | Documents the execution API. |\r\n| conventions/\u200bsrc/\u200btest/\u200bkotlin/\u200bio/\u200bopentelemetry/\u200binstrumentation/\u200bgradle/\u200bTestSuiteExecutionsTest.kt | Tests binding, ordering, metadata, and laziness. |\r\n| conventions/\u200bsrc/\u200bmain/\u200bkotlin/\u200botel.java-conventions.gradle.kts | Applies the execution plugin. |\r\n| conventions/\u200bsrc/\u200bmain/\u200bkotlin/\u200bio/\u200bopentelemetry/\u200binstrumentation/\u200bgradle/\u200bTestSuiteExecutions.kt | Implements execution registration and telemetry configuration. |\r\n| conventions/\u200bbuild.gradle.kts | Adds the JUnit platform launcher. |\r\n| .gitignore | Ignores Kotlin working files. |\n</details>\n\n\ud83e\udde0 **Review effort:** Balanced\n\n---\n\n\ud83d\udca1 <a href=\"/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation/new/main?filename=.github/skills/code-review/SKILL.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add a `code-review` agent skill</a> or configure MCP servers for context-aware, tailored reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/copilot/how-tos/use-copilot-agents/request-a-code-review/use-code-review?tool=webui#mcp-servers-and-agent-skills\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn more in the docs.</a>","comment_id":null,"key":"review:5538375750","kind":"body","line":null,"path":null,"review_id":5538375750},{"body":"[Testing] Wire these regression tests into PR CI. `conventions` is a separate included build (`settings.gradle.kts:127`), and root test partitioning visits only `subprojects` (`build.gradle.kts:105\u2013115`). The common workflow runs only `spotlessCheck` for `conventions`; its separate build job targets `gradle-plugins`. Consequently, these ordering, metadata-composition, and argument-provider assertions do not guard future changes. Add `./gradlew -p conventions test` to the PR workflow or explicitly wire the included build's test task into verification.","comment_commit_id":"16bd05cc5f11283e60da5870b883b5a69741fc70","comment_id":4287068923,"key":"inline:4287068923","kind":"inline","line":18,"original_commit_id":"16bd05cc5f11283e60da5870b883b5a69741fc70","original_line":18,"path":"conventions/src/test/kotlin/io/opentelemetry/instrumentation/gradle/TestSuiteExecutionsTest.kt","review_commit_id":"16bd05cc5f11283e60da5870b883b5a69741fc70","review_id":5538375750,"review_submitted_at":"2026-10-15T18:56:43Z","root_author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"thread_context":[{"author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"body_hash":"63a6693ee9aa7487a76c655c6da8342a3a7299dc0f194d16bb948d577ccc6fbe","id":4287068923,"parent":null,"updated_at":"2026-10-15T18:56:43Z"}],"thread_id":"PRRT_kwDODJKVX86s7BlH"}],"frozen_at":1792090950,"frozen_at_iso":"2026-10-15T19:02:30Z","frozen_sha":"16bd05cc5f11283e60da5870b883b5a69741fc70","head_ref":"copilot/build-gradle-test-infrastructure","head_repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","head_repo_id":210933087,"input_mode":"direct","launch_run":{"actor_id":218610,"attempt":1,"id":38790583362},"loop_kind":"copilot_review","metadata":{"body":"<!--\nCHANGELOG.md is generated from merged pull requests. Do not add an entry unless this PR introduces\na deprecation or breaking change.\n-->\n\nProposes suite-owned test executions to reduce variant boilerplate without copying configured `Test` tasks. This proof of concept adds reusable infrastructure and migrates only gRPC javaagent, preserving its default execution and all four variants.\n\n```kotlin\nexecutions {\n  configureEach {\n    jvmArgs(\"-Djava.net.preferIPv4Stack=true\")\n  }\n  register(\"Experimental\") {\n    telemetryConfig(\"otel.instrumentation.grpc.experimental-span-attributes\", \"true\")\n  }\n}\n```\n\n- **Ownership:** `JvmTestSuite` retains compilation and dependencies. Executions reuse its output and runtime classpath and join `check` automatically.\n- **Configuration:** Common settings precede variant settings regardless of declaration order. Each task receives shared conventions independently, preserving JVM argument providers without duplication.\n- **Telemetry:** `telemetryConfig` composes JVM properties and metadata conditions; variant values override common values. Ordinary JVM properties remain unlabeled.\n- **Scope:** Preserves gRPC task names, request-metadata settings, classpath filtering, dependency constraints, and latest-dependency/denyUnsafe behavior. Adds focused infrastructure coverage and contributor documentation; no other instrumentation migrations or general test matrix.","title":"Prototype suite-owned Gradle test executions with gRPC"},"mode":"publish","pr":20625,"pr_author_id":198982749,"protocol":"git-candidate-v1","publication":{"auth_mode":"fine_grained_pat","authorized_actor_id":218610,"authorized_at":1792090952,"generation":1,"max_pipelines":5,"phase":"7d98918838c64116818b8d96c75478d0","profile":"git-candidate-v1","required_checks":[]},"repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","repo_id":210933087,"request_id":"86630fd0785548288e4edd91cfb7b0e8","schema":2,"source_private":false,"target_private":false,"workflow_ref":"review-loop-revisions/1a211828aa1a2b731f5e9140623b5945a0dbdb6d","workflow_revision":"1a211828aa1a2b731f5e9140623b5945a0dbdb6d"},"run":{"attempt":1,"conclusion":"success","id":38790690799,"url":"https://github.com/trask/copilot-workflows/actions/runs/38790690799"},"schema":2,"seen_findings":["cbfd6d71489d9cca50ce08941540e81812209e2a92e9defcd310c472d49e6481"],"seen_inline_findings":["b81acc817780015e982847bdc23301cd39f3b68c84dd8ef35a75cdbd2e5a7cea"],"seen_missed_findings":[],"stage":"thread_effects","verification_run":{"attempt":1,"id":38793212771}}